[ISBK.3.4] **Order and atomicity.** libds validates every backend in a
registration before it registers any, so a bad entry registers nothing. Each
backend is checked in this order, and the first check it fails is the answer:

1. a missing vtable: `DS_ERR_INVAL`;
2. the ABI version ([ISBK.1.7]);
3. the backing ([ISBK.3.3]);
4. the aggregation set ([ISBK.3.2]);
5. the four required entry points ([ISBK.1]): `DS_ERR_INVAL`.

Once every entry passes, a backend for a backing already registered, or two for
one backing in the same registration, is `DS_ERR_STATE`, and nothing registers:
each backing has exactly one backend ([NSBK.2.3]). libds registers the seven
itself when it constructs an engine ([NSBK.2]), so an integrator meets none of
these codes but through a defect in libds.
